From: Manchego Stars engine
Subject: [PATCH] crit flourish (#11): a d20 pops on the crit-flash teardown

#11: the cosmetic nat-20 flourish. When an FE crit fires in a battle anim,
a d20 showing 20 pops on the effect layer (BG1) the exact frame the vanilla
crit flash tears down -- both the plain crit flash AND the pierce-crit flash
(Silencer is deliberately excluded: it has its own distinctive Chill flourish,
and no MVP cast member can Silencer anyway). FE crit math stays the SOLE
trigger: these teardowns only ever run on a crit round.

The die is PROC-LESS: registered once, then the vanilla effect lifecycle owns
BG1 -- a successor effect (brave second hit, magic counter's spell background)
simply draws over it, and the battle-scene exit resets the layer. Nothing of
ours ever clears BG1 later, so no lingering proc can blank a newcomer's
tilemap mid-display (the clobber class a timed teardown would create). It is
a centered HUD overlay copied through the non-mirrored tilemap path, so the
"20" never mirrors with attacker side. Asset symbols (Img/Pal/Tsa_MsD20Crit)
are injected from the campaign by inject.crit_flourish.inject_crit_flourish -- this
patch is campaign-agnostic.

Notes:

hook BOTH crit-flash teardowns (plain + pierce); the bare body appears in
more than one proc, so anchor on each enclosing function
---
diff --git a/src/banim-efxhit.c b/src/banim-efxhit.c
index 76c28b9c22578a38f60ab530946f107b3a13121b..d2b658b8ad36e16e7104dbd9a80a205c881c49f0 100644
--- a/src/banim-efxhit.c
+++ b/src/banim-efxhit.c
@@ -82,6 +82,25 @@ void efxDamageMojiEffectOBJMain(struct ProcEfxDamageMojiEffectOBJ * proc)
     }
 }
 
+#include "constants/video-banim.h" /* OBJPAL_BANIM_SPELL_BG (MS #11) */
+
+/* MS #11: cosmetic nat-20 flourish -- drawn once at a crit flash teardown;
+   the vanilla effect lifecycle owns BG1 from there (a successor effect
+   overwrites it, the scene exit resets it). */
+extern const u16 Img_MsD20Crit[];
+extern const u16 Pal_MsD20Crit[];
+extern const u16 Tsa_MsD20Crit[];
+
+static void MsD20CritShow(void)
+{
+    SpellFx_RegisterBgGfx(Img_MsD20Crit, 0x2000);
+    SpellFx_RegisterBgPal(Pal_MsD20Crit, 0x20);
+    LZ77UnCompWram(Tsa_MsD20Crit, gEkrTsaBuffer);
+    EfxTmCpyBG(gEkrTsaBuffer, gBG1TilemapBuffer, 30, 20,
+               OBJPAL_BANIM_SPELL_BG, 0x100);
+    BG_EnableSyncByMask(BG1_SYNC_BIT);
+}
+
 CONST_DATA struct ProcCmd ProcScr_efxCriricalEffect[] = {
     PROC_NAME("efxCriticalEffect"),
     PROC_REPEAT(efxCriricalEffectMain),
@@ -142,6 +161,7 @@ void efxCriricalEffectBGMain(struct ProcEfxBG * proc)
     if (++proc->timer == 0x11) {
         SpellFx_ClearBG1();
         SetDefaultColorEffects_();
+        MsD20CritShow(); /* MS #11: the nat-20 die takes the cleared layer */
         Proc_Break(proc);
     }
 }
@@ -373,6 +393,7 @@ void efxPierceCriticalEffectBGMain(struct ProcEfxBG * proc)
     if (++proc->timer == 0x11) {
         SpellFx_ClearBG1();
         SetDefaultColorEffects_();
+        MsD20CritShow(); /* MS #11: the nat-20 die takes the cleared layer */
         Proc_Break(proc);
     }
 }
